<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Pagaruyung Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1347 CE – 1833 CE (approx.) · capital Pagaruyung</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The royal seat of the Minangkabau of West Sumatra, founded by Adityawarman and destroyed in the Padri War of the 19th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1347 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adityawarman">Adityawarman</a>, a prince who had served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a>, proclaimed himself king of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/melayu-kingdom">Malayu</a> at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dharmasraya">Dharmasraya</a> and moved his court up into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minangkabau-people">Minangkabau</a> highlands, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pagaruyung">Pagaruyung</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanah-datar">Tanah Datar</a> valley. He left more than twenty inscriptions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-malay">Old Malay</a> and patronised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vajrayana">Tantric Buddhism</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Later rulers converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in the 16th century. Royal authority was shared among the Rajo Tigo Selo, three kings of the world, of custom and of religion, but real power lay with the village councils under matrilineal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adat">adat</a> law. Gold from highland mines made the court famous, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minangkabau-people">Minangkabau</a> migrants carried its prestige to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/negeri-sembilan">Negeri Sembilan</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padri-war">Padri War</a>, reformist Muslims killed much of the royal family around 1815. Surviving nobles invited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, who intervened from 1821. In 1833 the Dutch arrested the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-tangkal-alam-bagagar">Sultan Tangkal Alam Bagagar</a> and exiled him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavia">Batavia</a>, ending the kingdom. A replica palace stands at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pagaruyung">Pagaruyung</a> today.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/pagaruyung-kingdom.jpg" alt="Pagaruyung Kingdom" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: RahmatdenasMuffin Wizard This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Minang.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1347 CE – 1833 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pagaruyung</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Adityawarman, Sultan Arifin Muningsyah, Sultan Tangkal Alam Bagagar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, later Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Minangkabau, Malay</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Pagaruyung, Minangkabau Kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1590&amp;focus=pagaruyung-kingdom" aria-label="Pagaruyung Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7474 2194 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Pagaruyung Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7794 2450L7816 2473M7794 2450L7959 2663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7816 2473h0M7959 2663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7794 2450h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7794 2450h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1590&amp;focus=pagaruyung-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
